guest(i386nt) kernel driver which was written by LLM partialy(but i dominated the key part of procedure)


compiation:
  cd to your /path/to/qemu_ntivshmem/qemu_ntivhsmem/guest/i386nt/driver for Windows(WDM) and Linux(gcc)
  step 1 on host linux: i686-w64-mingw32-cc -c ./cusdriver_2.c -o cusdriver_2.obj
  step 2 on WDK(Windows): build
  create directory on Windows C:\CusDriverDir
  copy ./cusdriver.sys ./cusdriver.inf to C:\CusDriverDir
  cd C:\CusDriverDir
  go to device manager,install the inf,the device name usually named "PCI standard RAM controller"


